#! btw 1
#! name: the Assyrian, 122
#! license: CC0-1.0
#! visibility: public
# assyrian-122: the same deep house over an anapestic line (CC0-1.0; the words are Byron's, Hebrew Melodies, 1815, in the public
# domain). "The Assyrian came down like the wolf on the fold" is twelve syllables, two weak and a strong, four times. The book says
# its feel is triplet, so the voice and the shaker go in a cycle of twelve sixteenths, a 6/8 bar of three syllables to the beat
# against the four-on-the-floor kick, and come round together every three bars. The sections are twelve bars. Four passes, about
# six minutes.
arrange from template(deep-house, @byron_assyrian_wolf)
